# Ship Pull Request

One procedure for every PR in every repo. Repository differences are data, not
different steps — gates in `references/GATES.md`. A lone PR is a chain of one.

## Resolve

Never skip. List every PR in scope with base, draft state and check state
(`gh pr list --json number,baseRefName,headRefName,isDraft,mergeStateStatus,
statusCheckRollup`), look up each repo's gate, then order the work bottom-up
from the PR based on the default branch and process one at a time.

## Author

1. One branch, one purpose, branched from its base.
2. Rebase onto the base. Never merge the base into the branch.
3. Run the gate locally and see its exit code.
4. Write the body per `references/PR-BODY.md`.
5. Open as draft. Draft states a named, specific gap.

## Edit

When updating a PR's title, body, or base:
- Never use `gh pr edit` (`gh 2.45.0` fails on the deprecated Projects-classic
  GraphQL schema and silently leaves PR text stale).
- Use the REST PATCH path or the helper script:
  ```sh
  scripts/edit-pr.sh <number> --title "<title>" --body-file <path>
  # or directly with gh api:
  gh api -X PATCH repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<number> -f title="<title>" -F body=@<path>
  ```
- **Verification step (mandatory)**: check that the PR text updated by reading
  it back to detect and prevent stale-text failures:
  ```sh
  scripts/check-pr-text.sh <number> --title "<title>" --body-file <path>
  # or directly with gh api:
  gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<number> --jq '{title: .title, body: .body}'
  ```

## Ready

Leave draft only when every claim under Validation has run and its output was
seen. An unrun or failing claim stays under Residual risk and the PR stays
draft. Never promote on an agent's report alone. Promote with `gh pr ready <number>`,
and send title and body updates through the REST edit path and verify the saved text.

## Gate

- The reviewer re-runs the gate. Pasted output is not evidence.
- Review per `AGENTS.md` § Code review policy: one review of the integrated
  diff, P0-P3, verified findings only. Docs and skills self-review.
- Read the negative tests: each bypass needs a test that names it.
- A red check blocks that PR and everything above it. Fix the lowest failure.
- A failing gate on a non-draft PR returns it to draft.
- Close with `no known gap` or an explicit list, never a bare approval.

## Merge

Rebase-merge to linear history, then delete the branch. Never squash: squashing
discards the reviewed commits and replaces them with one no reviewer saw. Under
rebase the individual commit messages survive, so the PR body is the review
record, not the commit message. Never add `Co-Authored-By` AI-model lines. Then
rebase the next PR onto the merged base and re-gate it:
`references/STACKED-PRS.md`.

## Close out

- Close the originating issue from the merge, not by hand.
- Every unresolved Residual-risk item becomes a tracked issue at merge time.
- Downstream propagation (public mirror, package publish, release) is batched
  and owner-triggered, never part of merge. Commands in `references/GATES.md`.

